      "name": "ScrollBnetListUp",
      "signature": "int ScrollBnetListUp(int nUnused)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Scrolls the Battle.net list up by maximum amount.\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper - Calls FUN_6fa0a950 with -1 scroll delta.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set ECX = 0xFFFFFFFF (-1 as signed) for maximum upward scroll\n2. Call FUN_6fa0a950 to perform actual scroll operation\n3. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n- nUnused (int): Ignored stack parameter, present for handler signature compatibility\n\nReturns:\n- int: Always returns 1 (success)\n\nCalled By:\n- UI handler dispatch tables for scroll up events\n\nCalls:\n- FUN_6fa0a950: Battle.net list scroll position adjustment function\n\nNotes:\n- Uses RET 4 (__stdcall) to clean stack parameter\n- The -1 delta causes FUN_6fa0a950 to scroll toward list start\n- Parameter is unused but required for standard UI handler callback signature",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
