      "name": "SetInventoryPanelVisibility",
      "signature": "void SetInventoryPanelVisibility(int nShowPanel)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Shows or hides the inventory panel UI and manages related UI state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If nShowPanel == 0 (hide panel):\n   a. If mode is 0 and slot9 exists, clean up inventory UI elements\n   b. Call FUN_6fa10090 and FUN_6fa0f490 for panel cleanup\n   c. Dispatch handlers for all 10 inventory slots\n   d. Clear sub-children array via loop\n   e. Reset g_nNumSubChildren, g_dwInventorySubState, g_dwInventoryExtraState to 0\n   f. Call FUN_6fa117b0 for additional cleanup\n   g. If g_dwSpecialModeFlag == 1, call FUN_6fa127f0\n   h. If panel mode == 3, reset to 0\n   i. Set panel state bit mask if panel state exists\n   j. Check game list flags (0x1ea offset) for bit 8 and 4\n   k. Set button frame visibility based on DAT_6fa21894\n\n2. If nShowPanel != 0 (show panel):\n   a. Call Ordinal_10002 to check player character availability\n   b. If player not available (return 0):\n      - Validate string ID 0x14e7 (error message)\n      - Clean up existing sub-children\n      - Create inventory button, secondary button, and text box UI elements\n      - Store in g_apSubChildrenArray (max 32 elements, assert on overflow)\n      - Set callback to FUN_6fa054f0\n   c. If player available:\n      - Reset panel mode to 0\n      - Validate string ID 0x2a41\n      - Full cleanup of all inventory slots and sub-children\n      - Clear/set panel state bit masks\n      - Reset all button frame values to 0\n      - Create text box from g_TextBoxObjectType\n      - Set callback to ActivateInventoryPanelStateCallback\n\nParameters:\n  nShowPanel (ECX): 0 to hide panel, non-zero to show panel\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Assert fires if g_nNumSubChildren >= 32 (0x20) when adding elements\n  - Early return after creating text box in player-unavailable path\n  - Multiple redundant SetOrClearBitMask calls on g_pInventoryPanelState\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x14e7 - String ID for player unavailable message\n  0x2a41 - String ID for panel activation\n  0x1ea - Offset in game list data for feature flags\n  0x1086 - Source line number for max children assert\n  0x20 (32) - Maximum sub-children array capacity\n\nGlobal State Modified:\n  g_dwInventoryPanelMode, g_nNumSubChildren, g_dwInventorySubState,\n  g_dwInventoryExtraState, g_apSubChildrenArray, g_dwInventorySlot9,\n  _g_pfnSubPanelCallback",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
