      "name": "RestoreMcpConnectionState",
      "signature": "bool RestoreMcpConnectionState(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Restores MCP (Master Control Program) connection state after entering multiplayer lobby.\n\nClassification: Worker function - Called to restore saved game session connection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game list data has password flag at offset 0x225 set\n2. If flag is clear (no password required), return true immediately\n3. Check if callback vtable exists and call vtable[0x74] to validate MCP state\n4. Call D2MCPCLIENT.Ordinal_10002 to check if already connected\n5. If already connected, return true (no restoration needed)\n6. Clear password dialog cancelled flag (g_fPasswordDialogCancelled = 0)\n7. Load string ID 0x147b for password prompt\n8. Clean up existing sub-panel children (iterate g_apSubChildrenArray)\n9. Create password input button (g_UITypeInventoryButton)\n10. Create password label (g_UITypeInventoryLabel)\n11. Create text box element (type 0x21) for password entry\n12. Set sub-panel callback to PasswordSubPanelCallback\n13. Record timestamp in g_dwInventorySubState\n14. Call vtable[0x44] to get password data pointer\n15. If password data valid (>8 bytes), call D2MCPCLIENT.Ordinal_10000 with password\n16. Run message pump with MessagePumpPasswordCallback\n17. Clean up sub-panel children after password dialog\n18. If password not cancelled and MCP connected (Ordinal_10002) and not in error (Ordinal_10046 == 0):\n    a. Call D2MCPCLIENT.Ordinal_10009 with game name (g_pGameListData + 0xb8)\n    b. Run message pump with McpClientJoinGamePollCallback to poll join status\n    c. Clean up sub-panel children\n    d. Return inverse of Ordinal_10046 error state\n19. Otherwise clean up and return false\n\nParameters: None (uses global state)\n\nReturns:\n- true (1): MCP connection restored successfully or no restoration needed\n- false (0): Failed to restore MCP connection or user cancelled\n\nD2MCPCLIENT.DLL Ordinal Reference:\n- Ordinal_10000: SetMcpPassword - Set password for MCP authentication\n- Ordinal_10002: IsMcpConnected - Check if connected to MCP server\n- Ordinal_10009: JoinMcpGame - Request to join game via MCP\n- Ordinal_10046: GetMcpErrorState - Get current MCP error state (0 = no error)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns true immediately if password flag at g_pGameListData+0x225 is clear\n- Returns true if already connected (Ordinal_10002 returns non-zero)\n- Asserts if g_nNumSubChildren exceeds 0x1F (31) during UI element creation\n\nGlobal State Accessed:\n- g_pGameListData: Pointer to game list data structure\n- g_pCallbackVtable: Callback interface vtable pointer\n- g_nNumSubChildren: Count of sub-panel child elements\n- g_apSubChildrenArray: Array of sub-panel child pointers\n- g_fPasswordDialogCancelled: Flag set if user cancelled password dialog\n- g_dwInventorySubState: Timestamp/state for sub-panel\n- g_dwCurrentInputItem: Current input focus item\n- _g_pfnSubPanelCallback: Function pointer for sub-panel callbacks",
