      "name": "EditBoxKeyHandler",
      "signature": "uint EditBoxKeyHandler(uint dwUnused, size_t nCursorPosition, char * lpszKeyCode)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "EditBoxKeyHandler - Callback for handling special key presses in Battle.net chat edit box\n\nClassification: Callback/Handler - Invoked by edit control for special key events\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if key code is 0x0E (autocomplete trigger from chat history)\n2. If key is TAB (0x09):\n   a. Check if autocomplete entries exist (g_dwAutocompleteEntryCount != 0)\n   b. Increment current autocomplete index\n   c. Wrap index to 0 if exceeds entry count\n   d. Convert selected autocomplete entry to Unicode and set in edit box\n   e. Return 0 (handled)\n3. If key is not TAB and not 0x0E, return 1 (not handled)\n4. For 0x0E key (history insertion):\n   a. Get current edit box text via D2Win_GetEditBoxChild\n   b. If no text or no chat history buffer, return 0\n   c. Convert edit box Unicode text to ANSI (acStack_600)\n   d. Get history text from buffer (acStack_500)\n   e. Calculate combined length of current text + history text\n   f. If combined length exceeds 255 chars, return 0 (overflow protection)\n   g. Split current text at cursor position into prefix and suffix\n   h. Build new string: prefix + history + suffix using sprintf\n   i. Convert result to Unicode and update edit box\n5. Return 0\n\nParameters:\n  nUnused (uint) - Unused first parameter (stack-based calling convention padding)\n  nCursorPosition (size_t) - Current cursor position in edit box text\n  lpszKeyCode (char *) - Pointer to key code byte triggering callback\n\nReturns:\n  0 - Key was handled (TAB autocomplete or history insertion)\n  1 - Key was not handled (pass to default handler)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - TAB cycles through autocomplete entries with wraparound\n  - History insertion protects against buffer overflow (255 char limit)\n  - Empty edit box or missing history buffer causes early return\n  - Cursor position used to split text for inline history insertion\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n  g_dwAutocompleteEntryCount (0x6fa2188c) - Number of autocomplete entries\n  g_dwAutocompleteCurrentIndex (0x6fa1b04c) - Current autocomplete selection index\n  g_aszAutocompleteEntries (0x6fa20aa4) - Array of autocomplete strings (0x100 stride)\n  g_pChatHistoryBuffer (0x6fa21aa4) - Pointer to chat history data structure\n  g_pCurrentInputPointer - Current active edit control pointer",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
