      "name": "HandleReplyWhisperCommand",
      "signature": "int HandleReplyWhisperCommand(char * lpszInputCommand, char * lpszCommandPrefix)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Handles the /reply (or /r) whisper command to send private messages.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate lengths: strlen(lpszCommandPrefix), strlen(lpszInputCommand), \n   and verify input is at least as long as prefix\n2. Perform case-insensitive prefix comparison using ToUpperChar loop\n3. Check if command ends with space or null terminator at prefix boundary\n4. Check if g_szLastWhisperSender is empty (no previous whisper recipient)\n   - If empty, display \"Nobody to reply to!\" message and return 1\n5. Format command string with \"%s \" prefix pattern\n6. Copy input string to local_200 buffer\n7. Tokenize the input using space delimiter to extract target and message:\n   - First call FUN_6fa13275 (strtok-like) to get first token\n   - Second call to get message token\n   - If exactly 2 tokens found, proceed to send whisper\n8. If game is in online mode (callback vtable check returns true):\n   - Format whisper command as \"/w *%s %s\" and send via callback\n   - Return 1\n9. If offline/local mode:\n   - Validate string ID 0x14e7\n   - Clear existing sub-children controls\n   - Create UI panel with inventory button, secondary button, and text box\n   - Set CancelSubPanelAndStopMessageLoop as callback\n   - Return 1\n10. If token parsing fails (not exactly 2 tokens):\n    - Display \"Correct usage is: %s (message)\" help text\n    - Return 1\n11. If prefix doesn't match, return 0\n\nParameters:\n  lpszInputCommand (ECX) - Full command string from chat input (e.g., \"/r hello\")\n  lpszCommandPrefix (EDX) - Command prefix to match (e.g., \"/r\" or \"/reply\")\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Command was recognized and handled (success or displayed error message)\n  0 - Command prefix did not match, not handled\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty recipient (g_szLastWhisperSender empty): Shows \"Nobody to reply to!\"\n  - Missing message: Shows \"Correct usage is: %s (message)\"\n  - Online mode: Sends via network callback\n  - Offline mode: Creates local UI panel for message display",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
