      "name": "InitializeInventorySubPanelWithText",
      "signature": "void InitializeInventorySubPanelWithText(wchar_t * lpwszText, void * pfnCallback)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes inventory sub-panel with display text and optional callback.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Loop through existing sub-children and dispatch (destroy) each one\n2. Reset g_nNumSubChildren count to 0\n3. Call SetCurrentInputItem to restore input focus\n4. Reset g_dwInventorySubState to 0\n5. Assert sub-children count less than MAX_CHILDREN (31)\n6. Create button UI object via CreateObjectByTypeFactory\n7. Store button in g_apSubChildrenArray and increment count\n8. Call SetLastInventoryItem and SetUnitFlags on button\n9. Assert sub-children count less than MAX_CHILDREN\n10. Create label UI object via CreateObjectByTypeFactory\n11. Store label in g_apSubChildrenArray and increment count\n12. Call SetUnitFlags on label\n13. Assert sub-children count less than MAX_CHILDREN\n14. Create textbox UI object via CreateObjectByTypeFactory\n15. Store textbox in g_apSubChildrenArray and increment count\n16. Call SetUnitFlags on textbox\n17. Add display text to textbox via TextBoxAddText\n18. Set callback to pfnCallback or default FUN_6fa06a10 if NULL\n19. Store GetTickCount result in g_dwInventorySubState for timing\n\nParameters:\nlpwszText - Wide string text to display in the textbox panel\npfnCallback - Optional callback function for panel events (NULL uses default)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If pfnCallback is NULL, default callback FUN_6fa06a10 is used\n- Asserts and aborts if sub-children count exceeds 31 (MAX_CHILDREN)\n- Creates exactly 3 UI objects: Button, Label, TextBox\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x1F (31) - MAX_CHILDREN limit for sub-panel elements\n0x1086 (4230) - Source line number in ChatDlg.cpp for assert",
