      "name": "ResetInventorySubPanelState",
      "signature": "int ResetInventorySubPanelState(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Resets the inventory sub-panel state by cleaning up all child UI elements.\n\nClassification: Cleanup/Callback - invoked as g_pfnSubPanelCallback to reset panel state\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize loop counter to 0\n2. If g_nNumSubChildren > 0, iterate through g_apSubChildrenArray\n3. For each child, call DispatchInventoryItemHandler to clean up the UI element\n4. Increment counter and pointer, continue until all children processed\n5. Reset g_nNumSubChildren to 0\n6. Call SetCurrentInputItem with g_dwCurrentInputItem to restore input focus\n7. Reset g_dwInventorySubState to 0\n8. Return 1 (TRUE) indicating success\n\nParameters:\n  None (void)\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1 (TRUE)\n\nLocal Variables:\n  iVar1 (nChildIndex): Loop counter for iterating through children (int)\n  pdwInventoryType (pUIObject): Pointer to current UI object in array (uint *)\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n  g_nNumSubChildren @ 0x6fa21734: Count of child UI elements\n  g_apSubChildrenArray @ 0x6fa20a20: Array of child UI object pointers\n  g_dwCurrentInputItem @ 0x6fa216d0: Current input item ID\n  g_dwInventorySubState @ 0x6fa2173c: Sub-panel state/timestamp\n\nCallers:\n  Set as g_pfnSubPanelCallback by InitializeInventorySubPanel\n  Called from multiple UI functions for panel cleanup",
