      "name": "ResetButtonFrameStates",
      "signature": "int ResetButtonFrameStates(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Resets all button frame states and conditionally enables buttons based on game list flags.\n\nCalled during UI refresh to reset button visibility and interactivity states.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear button frame values - call SetButtonFrameValues with value 0 for frames 1, 3, 2, and 1 again\n2. Read game list flags from g_pGameListData + 0x1ea (ushort)\n3. If either bit 3 (0x08) OR bit 2 (0x04) is NOT set in flags:\n   a. Enable button frame 3 with mask type 1 via SetUnitBitMask\n   b. Enable button frame 2 with mask type 1 via SetUnitBitMask\n4. Always enable button frame 1 with mask type 1\n5. Set button frame 1 final state based on g_dwButtonFrame1State (1 if state==0, else 0)\n6. Return 1 (always succeeds)\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1 (success)\n\nFlag Bits at g_pGameListData + 0x1ea:\n  0x04 - Bit 2: Game list condition flag A\n  0x08 - Bit 3: Game list condition flag B\n  Both must be set to skip enabling frames 2 and 3\n\nGlobals Used:\n  g_pButtonFrame1 (0x6fa216c4) - Primary button frame pointer\n  g_pButtonFrame2 (0x6fa216c8) - Secondary button frame pointer  \n  g_pButtonFrame3 (0x6fa216c0) - Tertiary button frame pointer\n  g_pGameListData (0x6fa21728) - Game list data structure pointer\n  g_dwButtonFrame1State (0x6fa21894) - Button frame 1 state flag",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:05d8b4e6f04e4532fa5d976f8f07800a",
