      "name": "UpdateCharacterClassListScrollPosition",
      "signature": "int UpdateCharacterClassListScrollPosition(int nUnused)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Periodically scans text box lines for character class prefixes and updates scroll position.\n\nClassification: Timer/Callback - called periodically to sync UI display with character list\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current tick count and compare against g_dwPanelDisplayTimeout\n2. If timeout not elapsed or g_dwInventoryExtraState is null, exit early\n3. Get starting line number from GetTextBlockField58(g_dwInventoryExtraState)\n4. Calculate max scan range as min(startLine + 16, g_szCommandBufferEnd)\n5. For each line in range [startLine, maxLine):\n   a. Get line text via TextBoxGetLineChar\n   b. Convert Unicode to ANSI via Unicode::unicode2Win into local buffer\n   c. Compare against g_szCharacterClassPattern (\"-\" prefix for class abbrevs)\n   d. If match found (strcmp==0):\n      - Calculate page index: ((lineNum + rounding) >> 4) << 4\n      - Store to g_dwPanelStateA and jump to update\n6. After loop, if g_fClassListEnabled != 0, proceed to update\n7. If g_dwLastScrollPosition != g_dwPanelStateA:\n   a. Copy g_byPanelDisplayFlags to g_byPanelDisplayMode\n   b. Store g_dwPanelStateA to g_dwPanelStateB\n   c. Call Ordinal_10027 (D2Win scroll/display update)\n   d. Set next timeout to GetTickCount() + 1000ms\n   e. Update g_dwLastScrollPosition\n\nParameters:\n  nUnused (Stack+4) - int - Unused parameter (stdcall cleanup)\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1\n\nLocal Variables (Hungarian naming - function body incomplete in Ghidra):\n  DVar2 -> dwTickCount: DWORD from GetTickCount\n  nLineNum: int loop counter (already named)\n  iVar5 -> nStrCmpResult: int strcmp return value\n  iVar6 -> nMaxLineIndex: int max line to scan\n  pUVar3 -> pUnicodeLine: Unicode* line text pointer\n  pbVar4 -> pbLocalBuffer: byte* pointer into abStack_100\n  pbVar7 -> pbPattern: byte* pointer into g_szCharacterClassPattern\n  bVar1 -> byCurrentChar: byte current char being compared\n  bVar8 -> fCharLess: bool comparison flag\n  abStack_100 -> abAnsiBuffer: byte[256] ANSI conversion buffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit if tick count < g_dwPanelDisplayTimeout (rate limiting)\n- Early exit if g_dwInventoryExtraState is null\n- Character class pattern: \"-\\0\\0\\0asn\\0dru\\0bar\\0pal\\0nec\\0sor\\0ama\"\n- Page calculation rounds line number to nearest 16\n\nGlobals Modified:\n- g_dwPanelStateA: Target scroll position (page-aligned line number)\n- g_dwPanelStateB: Active scroll position being displayed\n- g_byPanelDisplayMode: Display mode byte\n- g_dwPanelDisplayTimeout: Next allowed update tick\n- g_dwLastScrollPosition: Cached last scroll position for change detection\n\nNOTE: Function body incomplete in Ghidra - only entry instruction visible.\nDecompiler produces correct output via flow analysis but variables cannot\nbe renamed via MCP tools. Run RecreateFunction_6fa06fe0.java script to fix.",
