      "name": "PopulateLadderPanelEntries",
      "signature": "void PopulateLadderPanelEntries(uint dwStartIndex, int nEntryCount, int nEntryStride, byte byDisplayFlags, int * pLadderEntryData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Populates ladder panel entries with player ranking data or displays \"not on ladder\" message.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Early exit if g_dwInventoryExtraState is null\n2. If nEntryCount == 0 (reset mode):\n   a. Initialize Unicode buffers (aUStack_200/400/600/700) for message formatting\n   b. Get player name via FUN_6fa11910\n   c. Format \"Player %s is not on the ladder\" message\n   d. Reset panel state: dispatch handlers for slots 1-10, clear sub-children\n   e. Reset inventory state flags and callback pointer\n   f. Handle special mode (g_dwSpecialModeFlag == 1) and panel mode 3\n   g. Clear button frames and create text box with formatted message\n3. If byDisplayFlags matches g_byPanelDisplayFlags (populate mode):\n   a. Navigate scrollbar to dwStartIndex if g_dwPanelStateA == -1\n   b. Initialize character class name array (ama/sor/nec/pal/bar/dru/ass)\n   c. Calculate end index (min of dwStartIndex+nEntryCount, g_szCommandBufferEnd)\n   d. For each entry from dwStartIndex to end index:\n      - Extract entry flags from pLadderEntryData[2]\n      - Compare entry name against g_szPanelDisplayText (highlight current player)\n      - Set line color (0 for match, 4 or 5 based on flags)\n      - Format rank number via FUN_6fa13454 to column 0\n      - Get character title via CalculateCharacterTitleTier (class, difficulty, expansion flags)\n      - Concatenate title + player name to column 1\n      - Set character class name to column 2 (from class name array)\n      - Format level to column 3\n      - Format experience as abbreviated number to column 4\n      - Advance entry pointer by nEntryStride + 0xC\n\nParameters:\n  dwStartIndex (ECX): Starting row index in ladder panel\n  nEntryCount (EDX): Number of entries to populate (0 = reset mode)\n  nEntryStride (Stack+0x4): Byte stride between ladder entries beyond fixed 12-byte header\n  byDisplayFlags (Stack+0x8): Display flags that must match g_byPanelDisplayFlags\n  pLadderEntryData (Stack+0xC): Pointer to ladder entry array\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nLadder Entry Structure (inferred at pLadderEntryData offset):\n  +0x00: Experience low dword\n  +0x04: Experience high dword  \n  +0x08: Flags dword (bits 0-3=class, 4=?, 5=expansion, 6=hardcore, 8-12=difficulty, 16-23=level)\n  +0x0C: Player name (null-terminated string)\n\nCharacter Class Mapping (bits 0-3):\n  0=Amazon, 1=Sorceress, 2=Necromancer, 3=Paladin, 4=Barbarian, 5=Druid, 6=Assassin\n\nFlag Bits in Entry Flags:\n  0x0F: Class mask (0-6)\n  0x10: Unknown flag (affects color)\n  0x20: Expansion character flag\n  0x40: Hardcore character flag\n  0x1F00: Difficulty mask (bits 8-12)\n\nText Columns:\n  0: Rank number\n  1: Title + Player name\n  2: Character class abbreviation\n  3: Character level\n  4: Experience (abbreviated)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
