      "name": "InitializePanelDisplayMode3",
      "signature": "void InitializePanelDisplayMode3(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initialize Panel Display Mode 3 (Class Selection)\n\nInitializes the panel display for mode 3, which appears to be a character class\nselection panel. Resets all button frames, enables slot 3 (selected), and\npopulates text content based on the current display flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Reset button frame values for slots 1-6 to 0 (unselected)\n2. If g_dwPanelResetFlag is set, also reset slots 7-8\n3. Set slot 3 button frame to 1 (selected state)\n4. If display flags are NOT 0x0B (11) or 0x02 (2):\n   a. Set command buffer size to 200 (0xC8)\n   b. Clear existing text data list\n   c. Initialize two Unicode buffer objects via constructor loop\n   d. Convert class code string to ANSI via FUN_6fa12b5e\n   e. Convert ANSI to Unicode via win2Unicode\n   f. Add text lines to panel with color 4 and flags 0\n   g. Navigate scrollbar to index 0\n   h. Set scroll offset to -2 (0xFFFFFFFE)\n   i. Enable class list (g_fClassListEnabled = 1)\n   j. Calculate panel mode base from display flags range:\n      - Flags 9-16 (0x09-0x10): base = 9\n      - Flags 19-26 (0x13-0x1A): base = 19\n      - Flags 27-34 (0x1B-0x22): base = 27\n      - Flags 0-7: base = 0\n      - Other: ASSERT failure and exit\n   k. Update display flags to (base + 2)\n   l. Clear panel state A\n5. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  None - This function takes no parameters\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Always returns success\n\nGlobals Modified:\n  g_szCommandBufferEnd (0x6fa214a4) - Set to 200\n  g_nPanelScrollOffset (0x6fa21740) - Set to -2\n  g_fClassListEnabled (0x6fa1b044) - Set to 1\n  g_dwPanelStateA (0x6fa1b058) - Set to 0\n  g_byPanelDisplayFlags (0x6fa1b054) - Updated to (base + 2)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x0B (11) - Panel mode: skip initialization\n  0x02 (2) - Panel mode: skip initialization  \n  0xC8 (200) - Command buffer size\n  0xFFFFFFFE (-2) - Initial scroll offset\n  0x09-0x10 (9-16) - Display flags range 1, base 9\n  0x13-0x1A (19-26) - Display flags range 2, base 19\n  0x1B-0x22 (27-34) - Display flags range 3, base 27\n  0x15F7 (5623) - Source file line number for assert",
