      "name": "InitializeChatPanelDisplayMode4",
      "signature": "int InitializeChatPanelDisplayMode4(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initializes chat panel display for mode 4 (character class selection variant).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Reset button frame values for panel slots 1-6 to disabled (0)\n2. If g_dwPanelResetFlag is set, also reset panel slots 7-8\n3. Enable panel slot 4 by setting its frame value to 1\n4. Early exit if display flags indicate modes 0x0C or 0x03 (already configured)\n5. Set command buffer size to 200 characters\n6. Clear existing text data from inventory extra state panel\n7. Initialize Unicode text buffer array (2 elements)\n8. Convert notification string (offset 0xA0 from base) to Unicode\n9. Add converted text lines to inventory extra state panel with 4 lines, flags 0\n10. Navigate scrollbar to index 0 (top)\n11. Read current display flags and mask to byte\n12. Set scroll offset to -2 (0xFFFFFFFE)\n13. Enable class list flag\n14. Determine base display mode from current flags:\n    - Flags 9-16 (0x09-0x10): base mode = 9\n    - Flags 0-7: base mode = 0\n    - Flags 19-26 (0x13-0x1A): base mode = 19\n    - Flags 27-34 (0x1B-0x22): base mode = 27\n    - Other values: Assert failure (line 5623 in ChatDlg.cpp)\n15. Clear panel state A\n16. Set display flags to (base mode + 3)\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: 1 (TRUE) on success, does not return on invalid display flags\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_byPanelDisplayFlags is 0x0C or 0x03, function exits early returning 1\n- Invalid display flag ranges trigger FogAssert and non-returning exit\n\nDisplay Flag Ranges:\n- 0x00-0x07: Base mode 0, sets flags to 0x03\n- 0x09-0x10: Base mode 9, sets flags to 0x0C  \n- 0x13-0x1A: Base mode 19, sets flags to 0x16\n- 0x1B-0x22: Base mode 27, sets flags to 0x1E\n\nSource: ChatDlg.cpp line 5623",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
