      "name": "BnetAdHandler_StubReturnTrue",
      "signature": "int BnetAdHandler_StubReturnTrue(char * lpszStringBuffer, char * lpszStringEnd)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Stub handler for Battle.net advertisement message type 0 (string handler).\n\nClassification: Callback/Handler - invoked via g_apfnBnetAdHandlers[0] dispatch.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Return TRUE (1) unconditionally, ignoring all parameters\n\nParameters:\n  lpszStringBuffer - Pointer to null-terminated advertisement string (ignored)\n  lpszStringEnd - Pointer to end of string buffer (ignored)\n\nReturns:\n  1 (TRUE) - Always succeeds\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  This is a no-op stub handler at index 0 in the Battle.net ad handler table.\n  All string content is discarded without processing.\n\nCross-References:\n  Called from ProcessBnetAdvertisementData when nMessageType==0 and dwParam==0\n  Function pointer stored at g_apfnBnetAdHandlers[0] (0x6fa1d79c)",
