      "name": "DisplayFormattedChatPlayerName",
      "signature": "void DisplayFormattedChatPlayerName(dword dwTextColor)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Formats and displays player name with title prefix in chat text box.\n\nCLASSIFICATION: Worker function - formats chat sender name with game status\n\nALGORITHM:\n1. Call FUN_6fa12ce0 to allocate stack frame (0x1110 bytes)\n2. Get current player name from callback vtable[0x18]\n3. Copy player name to local buffer (stack0x10)\n4. Initialize color code to 4 (default white)\n5. Search g_pGameListHead linked list for matching player:\n   a. For each game entry, find '*' in name at offset +4\n   b. If '*' found with text after, use text after '*' as name\n   c. Otherwise use full name from offset +4\n   d. Compare name against local buffer (inline strcmp)\n   e. If match found:\n      - Copy game entry name to local buffer\n      - Check game flags at offset +0x90:\n        - Flag 0x02 set: color = 0 (hostile/red)\n        - Flag 0x01 or 0x08 set: color = 3 (special/yellow)\n        - Otherwise: keep color = 4\n6. Call FUN_6fa0d100 to parse name, title, and channel info\n7. Check if title string (stack0x110) is non-empty:\n   a. If title AND channel both non-empty: format as \"<%s%s> \" (name+title)\n   b. Otherwise: format as \"<%s> \" (name only)\n8. Initialize Unicode buffers (0x240 wchar_t each at stack0x410, stack0x890)\n9. Convert formatted name and message to Unicode via win2Unicode\n10. Validate Unicode name length < 500 chars (assert on overflow)\n11. Get string ID 0xF9A (color prefix) and strip from name buffer\n12. Strip color prefix from message buffer similarly\n13. Call FUN_6fa0e5f0 to prepend color code to name\n14. Initialize temp Unicode buffers (0x200 at stack0xd10, 3 chars at stack0x8)\n15. Get string ID 0xF9A again, copy to temp, append formatted number\n16. Build final display string:\n    a. If name buffer empty: copy prefix directly\n    b. Otherwise: validate length < 500, append prefix\n17. Append message buffer to name buffer\n18. Display via CharSelectTextBoxAddText with color code\n\nPARAMETERS:\n  dwTextColor (stack+0x4) - Unused parameter, overwritten to 0 then reused for color\n\nRETURNS:\n  void\n\nSPECIAL CASES:\n  - Player name with '*' prefix uses text after '*' as display name\n  - Empty title uses simpler \"<%s> \" format\n  - Unicode length >= 500 triggers FogAssert and aborts\n\nGLOBALS ACCESSED:\n  g_pCallbackVtable (0x6fa20a1c) - UI callback vtable pointer\n  g_pGameListHead (0x6fa21a90) - Head of game/player linked list\n\nMAGIC NUMBERS:\n  0x1110 - Stack frame size\n  0x240 - Unicode buffer size (576 wchar_t)\n  0x200 - Temp Unicode buffer size (512 wchar_t)\n  0x2a - ASCII '*' character\n  0xf9a - String ID for color prefix\n  0x1f4 - Max Unicode length (500 decimal)\n  0x2e4 - Assert line number (740 decimal)\n  0xae7 - Assert line number (2791 decimal)\n\nFLAG BITS (offset +0x90):\n  0x01 - Special game mode flag\n  0x02 - Hostile/enemy flag\n  0x08 - Alternative special flag",
