      "name": "FormatAndDisplayChatMessage",
      "signature": "int FormatAndDisplayChatMessage(char * lpszPlayerName, char * lpszMessageText)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Formats and displays a chat message in the character select text box.\n\nCallback function (referenced from function pointer table at 0x6fa1d7b0).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Parse player name to extract base name and title using ParseChatPlayerNameAndTitle\n2. Initialize color code to 4 (default) and style to 0\n3. Search g_pGameListHead linked list for matching player name\n4. If player found, check flags at offset +0x90:\n   - Flag 0x02 set: Set color code to 0 (white/normal)\n   - Flag 0x01 or 0x08 set: Set color code and style to 3 (special)\n5. Check if player has title (acStack_880 not empty):\n   - If no title: Format with name only using szFmtNameOnly\n   - If has title: Format with name and title using szFmtNameWithTitleConcat\n6. Initialize Unicode buffers aUStack_d00 and aUStack_480 (1152 elements each)\n7. Convert formatted name to Unicode in aUStack_d00\n8. Convert message text to Unicode in aUStack_480\n9. Validate string length does not exceed 499 characters (assert if exceeded)\n10. Strip color code pattern (string ID 0xf9a) from both name and message strings\n11. Call PrependColorCodeToUnicodeString to add color prefix based on player type\n12. Call AppendColorCodeToUnicodeString to add color suffix\n13. Concatenate message text to formatted name\n14. Display final string via CharSelectTextBoxAddText\n\nParameters:\n    lpszPlayerName - Player name string (may include title prefix)\n    lpszMessageText - Chat message text to display\n\nReturns:\n    1 - Always returns success\n\nSpecial Cases:\n    - Empty title: Uses szFmtNameOnly format (\"%s\")\n    - Player with title: Uses szFmtNameWithTitleConcat (\"%s%s\") or composite\n    - String over 499 chars: Triggers FogAssert and terminates\n\nPlayer Flags (offset +0x90 in game list entry):\n    0x01 - Special player type (sets color 3)\n    0x02 - Operator/privileged player (sets color 0)\n    0x08 - Alternative special type (sets color 3)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n    0x240 - Unicode buffer size (576 elements = 1152 bytes)\n    499 - Maximum string length before assert\n    0xf9a - String ID for color code pattern to strip\n    0xa0 - Offset to next pointer in game list node\n    0x90 - Offset to player flags in game list node\n    4 - Offset to player name in game list node\n\nNote: Function has broken boundaries in Ghidra (shows as single instruction).\nDecompiler successfully analyzes full function body 0x6fa0d280-0x6fa0d6c8.",
