      "name": "AppendColorCodeToUnicodeString",
      "signature": "void AppendColorCodeToUnicodeString(Unicode * pDstString, uint dwColorCode)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Appends a color code escape sequence to a Unicode string buffer.\n\nRetrieves the color prefix string (string ID 0xF9A), converts the color code\nvalue to a numeric string, then appends the combined color escape sequence\nto the destination string. Enforces a 499 character length limit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize local Unicode buffer (1024 elements) with default constructors\n2. Initialize small Unicode buffer (8 elements) for color code conversion\n3. Retrieve color prefix string via ValidateStringId(0xF9A)\n4. Copy color prefix to local buffer\n5. Convert dwColorCode to ANSI string using wsprintfA with \"%d\" format\n6. Convert ANSI color code to Unicode (2 chars max)\n7. Concatenate Unicode color code to local buffer\n8. If destination string is empty (first char == 0):\n   - Copy entire color prefix buffer to destination\n   - Return\n9. Check destination string length\n10. If length >= 500:\n    - Assert failure (szAssertUnicodeStrlenLimit)\n    - Call FUN_6fa12bdd(-1) which does not return\n11. Concatenate color prefix buffer to existing destination string\n\nParameters:\n  pDstString - [in/out] Pointer to destination Unicode string buffer\n  dwColorCode - [in] Color code value to append (converted to decimal string)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty destination: Copies color prefix directly instead of concatenating\n  - Length >= 500: Triggers assertion failure and terminates\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xF9A (3994) - String ID for color prefix escape sequence\n  0x200 (512) - Loop count for 1024-element buffer init (512 * 2 bytes)\n  499 (0x1F3) - Maximum allowed string length before assert\n  0xAE7 (2791) - Line number in ComCallback.cpp for assert",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:c605e29ee6b728ad4fd7c86dfda98b43",
