      "name": "ValidateEditBoxTextAndSetMask",
      "signature": "int ValidateEditBoxTextAndSetMask(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Validates edit box text content and sets UI element bit mask based on text presence.\nCalled as callback when edit box content changes. Checks if game name field has text.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve Unicode text from g_pGameNameEditBox via D2Win_GetEditBoxChild\n2. If text pointer is NULL, set mask type to 0 (no text)\n3. Convert Unicode to ANSI using unicode2Win with 255 char max\n4. Calculate string length using REPNE SCASB pattern:\n   - Initialize counter to -1 (0xFFFFFFFF)\n   - Scan for null terminator, decrement counter each byte\n   - NOT and DEC to get actual length\n5. If string length >= 1, set mask type to 1 (has valid text)\n6. Call SetUnitBitMask on g_pGameListContainer with mask type\n7. Always return 1 (TRUE) indicating callback handled\n\nParameters: None (uses global UI state)\n\nReturns: Always 1 (TRUE) - callback success indicator\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL text pointer: Sets mask to 0 without string processing\n- Empty string (length 0): Sets mask to 0\n- Any text >= 1 char: Sets mask to 1\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n- g_pGameNameEditBox (0x6fa3e8d4): Edit box control for game name input\n- g_pGameListContainer (0x6fa3e8cc): UI container receiving the bit mask update",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
