      "name": "ShutdownBnetMultiplayerUI",
      "signature": "int ShutdownBnetMultiplayerUI(int nUnused)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Shuts down the Battle.net multiplayer UI and resets all associated state.\n\nClassification: Cleanup wrapper - Orchestrates UI shutdown sequence.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call ResetButtonFrameStates() - Clear button frame values and reset enable states\n2. Call ShutdownMcpClient() - Disconnect MCP client and release connection resources\n3. Call ResetBnetUIElements() - Dispatch handlers for all Bnet UI widgets and restore input focus\n4. Return 1 (TRUE) indicating successful shutdown\n\nParameters:\n  nUnused (int) - Unused parameter, passed via stack (RET 4 cleanup)\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1 (TRUE) for successful shutdown\n\nCalling Convention: __stdcall (RET 4 cleanup observed in disassembly)\n\nCallers:\n  - Referenced from data at 0x6fa1ce50 (likely function pointer table)\n\nCallees:\n  - ResetButtonFrameStates: Resets button frame states and enables based on game list flags\n  - ShutdownMcpClient: Calls D2MCPCLIENT ordinals 10054/10053 for MCP cleanup\n  - ResetBnetUIElements: Dispatches inventory handlers for 30+ UI widgets\n\nNotes:\n  Simple cleanup orchestrator that ensures proper shutdown order for\n  Battle.net multiplayer UI components. Called via function pointer\n  during panel state transitions.",
