      "name": "SetBnetGameListHellDifficulty",
      "signature": "bool SetBnetGameListHellDifficulty(void * pUnused)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Sets Battle.net game list panel to Hell difficulty mode (difficulty level 2).\n\nClassification: Initialization function (UI state configuration)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set g_pBnetGameListPanel button frame to 0 (inactive state)\n2. Set g_pBnetGameListScrollUp button frame to 0 (inactive)\n3. Set g_pBnetGameListScrollDown button frame to 1 (active/highlighted)\n4. Set g_nDifficultyLevel to 2 (Hell difficulty)\n5. Set byte at offset 0x20B in g_pGameListData to 2 (difficulty filter flag)\n6. Return TRUE (1)\n\nParameters:\n- pUnused (void *): Unused parameter, passed on stack (stdcall convention)\n\nReturns:\n- bool: Always returns TRUE (1) indicating success\n\nGlobals Modified:\n- g_nDifficultyLevel (0x6fa3e9dc): Set to 2\n- g_pGameListData->field_20B: Set to 2 (difficulty filter)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- ResetGameListPanelButtonStates (0x6fa110d0): Sets difficulty 0 (Normal)\n- InitializeBnetGameListDefaults (0x6fa11120): Sets difficulty 1 (Nightmare)\n- SetBnetGameListHellDifficulty (this): Sets difficulty 2 (Hell)\n\nNote: Function body appears malformed in Ghidra (single instruction boundary).\nActual code spans 0x6fa11170-0x6fa111b6 based on byte analysis ending at RET 4.",
