      "name": "InitializeCodePageLocale",
      "signature": "int InitializeCodePageLocale(int nCodePageId)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Sets the character type table for a specified code page.\n\nInitializes g_abCharTypeTable with character type flags based on either a known\ncode page from the internal lookup table or by querying Windows GetCPInfo API.\nUsed by CRT locale routines to classify characters for MBCS processing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Enter critical section 0x19 for thread safety\n2. Resolve code page ID via FUN_6fa1682e (-3=ACP, -2=OEMCP, -4=default)\n3. If code page matches current (g_dwCurrentCodePage), return 0 (success)\n4. If code page is 0, call FUN_6fa168ab to reset to default\n5. Search g_adwKnownCodePages array (5 entries at 0x30-byte stride) for match\n6. If found in known table:\n   a. Clear g_abCharTypeTable (257 bytes) to zero\n   b. Apply character type masks from table (4 categories at 8-byte stride)\n   c. For each character range pair [start,end], OR in type mask\n   d. Set g_fMultiByteCodePage=1, store code page, get LCID via FUN_6fa16878\n   e. Copy 3 dwords of code page parameters\n7. If not found, call GetCPInfo to query Windows:\n   a. If failed and g_fCodePageFallbackEnabled=0, return -1 (error)\n   b. Clear g_abCharTypeTable to zero\n   c. If MaxCharSize<2: single-byte code page, g_fMultiByteCodePage=0\n   d. If MaxCharSize>=2: multi-byte code page\n      - Mark lead byte ranges with flag 0x04 from LeadByte pairs\n      - Mark all bytes 1-254 with flag 0x08 (valid trail bytes)\n      - g_fMultiByteCodePage=1, get LCID via FUN_6fa16878\n   e. Clear code page parameters to 0\n8. Call FUN_6fa168d4 to finalize locale update\n9. Leave critical section, return 0 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  nCodePageId [int, in]: Code page identifier\n    -3: Use system ANSI code page (GetACP)\n    -2: Use system OEM code page (GetOEMCP)\n    -4: Use default code page from g_dwDefaultCodePage\n    >0: Specific code page number (e.g., 932, 936, 949, 950)\n\nReturns:\n  0: Success - character type table initialized\n  -1: Failure - GetCPInfo failed and no fallback enabled\n\nGlobals Modified:\n  g_dwCurrentCodePage (0x6fa3ed74): Current active code page\n  g_abCharTypeTable (0x6fa3eea0): 257-byte character type lookup table\n  g_fMultiByteCodePage (0x6fa3ed8c): Flag: 1=MBCS, 0=SBCS\n  g_dwCodePageLCID (0x6fa3efa4): Locale ID for code page\n  g_dwCodePageParam1-3: Code page specific parameters\n\nCharacter Type Flags (ORed into g_abCharTypeTable):\n  0x04: Lead byte in multi-byte character sequence\n  0x08: Valid trail byte in multi-byte character sequence\n\nKnown Code Pages Table (g_adwKnownCodePages at 0x6fa1e438):\n  Entry stride: 0x30 (48) bytes\n  +0x00: Code page number\n  +0x04: Unknown param 1\n  +0x08: Unknown param 2\n  +0x0C: Unknown param 3\n  +0x10: Character range table pointer (4 categories x 8 bytes)",
