      "name": "ValidateStreamPropertyId",
      "signature": "void ValidateStreamPropertyId(uint dwDosError)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Maps a Windows/DOS error code to a C runtime errno value.\n\nClassification: Utility/Internal - CRT error translation helper\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get pointer to _doserrno via CRT_GetDosErrnoPtr()\n2. Store dwDosError in _doserrno for later retrieval\n3. Initialize loop counter nMapIndex = 0, pointer pdwMapEntry to g_adwDosErrnoMap\n4. LOOP: Compare dwDosError against DOS error at current map entry\n   4a. If match found: get errno pointer, set *errno = g_adwErrnoValues[nMapIndex], return\n   4b. Advance pdwMapEntry by 8 bytes (2 DWORDs), increment nMapIndex\n   4c. Continue while pdwMapEntry < g_pDosErrnoMapEnd\n5. If 0x13 <= dwDosError <= 0x24 (DOS extended error range): set errno = EACCES (0x0D)\n6. If 0xBC <= dwDosError <= 0xCA (resource/memory errors): set errno = ENOMEM (0x08)\n7. Default: set errno = EINVAL (0x16)\n\nParameters:\n  dwDosError (uint, Stack[0x4]) - Windows/DOS error code to translate\n\nReturns:\n  void - Sets global errno and _doserrno as side effects\n\nError Code Mapping Table (g_adwDosErrnoMap at 0x6fa20558):\n  Stride: 8 bytes per entry (DOS error DWORD, errno DWORD)\n  Format: [DOS_ERROR, ERRNO] pairs\n  Count: 45 entries (0x168 bytes / 8 = 45)\n  \nSpecial Range Mappings:\n  0x13-0x24: Extended DOS errors -> EACCES (0x0D, permission denied)\n  0xBC-0xCA: Resource errors -> ENOMEM (0x08, not enough memory)\n  Default fallback: EINVAL (0x16, invalid argument)\n\nCommon errno values:\n  0x02 = ENOENT (no such file/directory)\n  0x07 = E2BIG (argument list too long)\n  0x08 = ENOMEM (not enough memory)\n  0x09 = EBADF (bad file descriptor)\n  0x0C = ENOMEM (not enough core)\n  0x0D = EACCES (permission denied)\n  0x11 = EEXIST (file exists)\n  0x12 = EXDEV (cross-device link)\n  0x16 = EINVAL (invalid argument)\n\nCallers:\n  CRT_lseek_nolock, CRT_write_nolock, FUN_6fa1823e",
